{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/4/* 2>/dev/null\"","aggregated_output":"<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据每个矩形框内的标记像素朝向，确定该框应与哪个方向上的同色锚点配对，然后用锚点颜色填充框的内部。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中有若干个由 Grey 像素构成的一像素厚空心矩形框。\n  - 每个框的某一条边上有恰好一个非 Grey、非 Black 的彩色标记像素（如 Red、Blue、Green），嵌在边框像素中，替换了该位置的 Grey 像素。\n  - 网格中另有若干个 2x2 的彩色实心锚点方块散布在框外，锚点颜色与某些框的标记颜色相同。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个矩形框，确定其标记像素所在的边（上、下、左、右），该边指向框外的方向即为\"朝向\"。\n  - 沿朝向方向寻找第一个与标记同色的 2x2 锚点方块。\n  - 将该矩形框内部（不含边框）的所有背景像素填充为锚点的颜色。\n  - 保持框的 Grey 边框、标记像素、锚点方块不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：标记像素所在的边既编码了搜索方向，又通过颜色指定了配对锚点；解题者需要同时归纳方向编码和颜色配对两层规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将每对同色对象之间的空白区域填充为第三种颜色，填充颜色由两个对象之间是否存在\"桥梁\"对象决定。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Azure。\n  - 网格中有若干对同色的 4-连通矩形对象（如两个 Red 矩形、两个 Blue 矩形等），每对对象在同一行或同一列上对齐。\n  - 某些同色对之间的背景区域中存在一个 Grey 的小型\"桥梁\"对象（1-2 像素），某些同色对之间没有桥梁。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每对同行/同列对齐的同色矩形对象：\n    - 如果两者之间的背景间隙中存在 Grey 桥梁对象，则用 Yellow 填充两者之间的整个矩形间隙区域（包括覆盖桥梁）。\n    - 如果两者之间没有桥梁，则用 Maroon 填充两者之间的整个矩形间隙区域。\n  - 保持原始矩形对象和未配对区域不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：同色对之间的桥梁存在与否是一个布尔判断，它选择两种不同的填充颜色；解题者需要先识别同色配对关系，再发现桥梁的控制作用。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：从多个部分重叠的彩色层中，提取每层的完整矩形轮廓，并将所有层按面积从大到小重新绘制为左对齐的并排竖条。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中有若干个不同颜色的实心矩形区域，部分矩形相互重叠。重叠处只显示最上层的颜色。\n  - 每种颜色的可见像素范围足以推断出该颜色完整矩形的宽度和高度。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每种前景颜色，从其所有可见像素的 bbox 推断出完整矩形的宽度 W 和高度 H。\n  - 按矩形面积（W*H）从大到小排列。\n  - 在输出画布上，从左到右依次绘制每个矩形，底部对齐，矩形之间间隔一列背景色。\n  - 每个矩形用其原始颜色完整绘制（不再有遮挡）。\n\n- `Key insight`：重叠区域的可见像素不影响 bbox 推断；输出丢弃了所有位置信息，仅保留面积排序和原始颜色。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将每个前景形状的像素\"折叠\"到其对称轴上，折叠后重叠的像素用新颜色标记。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中有若干个 4-连通单色前景对象，每个对象具有唯一的反射对称轴（水平或垂直）。\n  - 对象的像素分布在对称轴两侧，但两侧不完全对称——某些像素只存在于一侧。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个对象，找到其最佳反射对称轴。\n  - 将对称轴一侧的所有像素反射到另一侧。\n  - 如果反射后的像素位置已有同色像素（即对称的那部分），将该位置的像素重着色为 Yellow。\n  - 如果反射后的像素位置为背景色（即非对称的那部分），在该位置用原色绘制。\n  - 原始位置的像素保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：对称轴不是显式给出的，需要从对象形状中推断；Yellow 标记的是\"已对称\"的像素对，而新增像素是\"修复对称\"的结果——两层信息编码在同一个输出中。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：在网格中的多个容器对象内，根据容器的边数（三角形/矩形/五边形轮廓）从图例中选择对应的填充图案，将图案平铺到容器内部。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格下方有一行图例区域，包含三个由 Grey 分隔的小方格，每个方格内有一个简单的 2x2 彩色图案（如棋盘格、条纹、实心等），分别对应 3 边、4 边、5 边轮廓。\n  - 网格上方有若干个由不同颜色的一像素厚线段围成的封闭多边形轮廓（近似三角形、矩形或五边形），轮廓在网格上以直角折线近似绘制。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 数出每个轮廓的\"角\"数（即轮廓线段的方向变化点数量），得到等效边数。\n  - 从图例中找到对应边数的 2x2 图案。\n  - 将该图案以周期平铺方式填充到轮廓内部的背景像素上。\n  - 保持轮廓线和图例不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：轮廓的角数（而非面积或颜色）是选择图案的索引；解题者需要先归纳角数与图例位置的对应关系，再理解平铺填充机制。\n</new_puzzle>\ntrain/7e576d6e\neval/a395ee82\neval/f931b4a8\ntrain/c4d1a9ae\ntrain/57edb29d\ntrain/b1986d4b\ntrain/42f14c03\neval/db695cfb\ntrain/fc10701f\ntrain/a644e277\ntrain/6ca952ad\ntrain/9f669b64\ntrain/a09f6c25\ntrain/cf5fd0ad\ntrain/f0100645\neval/2b83f449\neval/97d7923e\ntrain/5587a8d0\neval/7b80bb43\ntrain/9720b24f\n你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"7e576d6e\" lines=\"159-181\">\n<description>\nDraw the marker-colored route through the centers of all doors in the parallel wall maze.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a background, parallel full-span walls, one three-pixel door\n  segment in each wall, and two marker pixels sharing a color.\n- Walls are either all vertical or all horizontal, and the markers are on\n  opposite outer sides of the wall set.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the scene unchanged except for the route.\n- Visit the door centers in wall order from the upper/left marker side to\n  the lower/right marker side.\n- In each corridor, draw an orthogonal path to the cell just before the next\n  wall, move along that wall to the door center, cross the center, and\n  continue to the next corridor; after the last door, connect to the other\n  marker.\n\nKey insight:\n- The three-pixel door segments mark the only crossing points through a set\n  of parallel walls, so the output is the corridor path threaded through\n  those centers.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a395ee82\" lines=\"9-24\">\n<description>\nStamp translated copies of a monochrome template guided by a singleton pixel layout.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background. A large monochrome shape (template, color T).\n- Singleton pixels elsewhere: exactly one is color T (layout origin); the rest share color O (overlap color).\n- Singletons sit on a uniform-spacing lattice.\n\nRule:\n- Convert each singleton's offset from the origin into coarse lattice units.\n- Place a template copy at each offset, scaled by template height/width.\n- The origin's copy is painted O instead of T.\n- Any pixel covered by two or more copies is also recolored to O.\n\nKey insight: The single T-colored singleton identifies both the origin position and the \"self\" copy, which is uniquely recolored.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"f931b4a8\" lines=\"10-27\">\n<description>\nCount the two upper quadrant control regions to size an output made from the lower quadrant pattern.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is an even square split into four equal quadrants.\n- Black is the background.\n- The upper-left and upper-right quadrants are control regions.\n- The lower-left quadrant is a color source tile; the lower-right quadrant is either a stencil tile or empty.\n\nRule:\n- Output height is the number of non-background pixels in the upper-left quadrant.\n- Output width is the number of non-background pixels in the upper-right quadrant.\n- If the lower-right stencil has foreground pixels, tile it over the output; each stencil background pixel is filled from the lower-left quadrant cell at the corresponding coarse tile position.\n- If the lower-right stencil is empty, tile the lower-left quadrant directly over the output.\n\nKey insight:\n- The top quadrants specify only dimensions, while the bottom quadrants specify a two-level repeated pattern: a fine stencil and coarse fill colors.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"c4d1a9ae\" lines=\"28-48\">\n<description>\nFill each vertical foreground band's background cells with the color of the next band to its right.\n\nInput structure\n- The dominant color is the background.\n- Each other color occupies a separate vertical band defined by that color's\n  minimum and maximum columns.\n- Within a band, all cells are either that band's color or background.\n\nRule\n- Order the bands from left to right.\n- In each band, replace background pixels with the color of the next band in\n  that order, wrapping from the rightmost band back to the leftmost.\n- Preserve all existing foreground pixels and all background pixels outside\n  the bands.\n\nKey insight\n- The column bands form a cyclic palette legend: a band's gaps are completed\n  by borrowing the color from its right-hand neighbor, not by changing the\n  band's existing pixels.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"57edb29d\" lines=\"88-103\">\n<description>\nExtract the single plain rectangle and redraw it with the aligned rectangles' border-relative marker pattern.\n\nInput structure:\n- The boundary color is the background/separator.\n- Foreground objects are dense rectangular regions; exactly one rectangle has only its base color.\n- Other rectangles contain their base color plus marker pixels.\n\nRule:\n- Crop the only plain rectangle; this crop is the output canvas.\n- Use marked rectangles whose row span overlaps the plain rectangle's row span.\n- Transfer their marker pixels by preserving each marker run's distance from the nearest rectangle edges.\n\nKey insight:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
